course: dictionary
lesson: 16113
title: Comparing with wetter
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Wet means it has water on it or in it. Add -er to compare two things: wetter means more wet than something else. «The sponge is wet, but the towel is wetter.» Both are wet, but the towel has more water in it.
explain: With short words like wet, you double the last letter before adding -er: wet, wetter, wettest. Wetter always compares two things. For three or more, use wettest.
explain: Wetter can also describe weather. «It is getting wetter outside, so take your coat.» It means there is more rain now than before. In science, you can test which material soaks up more water and is wetter.
fact: Wetter is the comparative form of wet: wet, wetter, wettest.
fact: «Wetter» means more wet, with more water on it or in it.
fact: «Wetter» can also mean there is more rain: «The west of Ireland is wetter than the east.»
fact: When a short word ends in one vowel and one consonant, double the consonant before -er: wet becomes wetter.
fact: Comparing two things uses -er (wetter), and comparing three or more things uses -est (wettest).
exercise: My hair is wet, but yours is dripping. Yours is ___. | weter | wet | *wetter | wettest
exercise: «The sand near the sea is wetter than the sand at the top of the beach.» What does wetter mean here? | Less wet, and drier | Very cold | *More wet, with more water in it | Full of stones
exercise: Which word is correct to compare two puddles? | wetest | wettest | *wetter | weter
test: «After the storm, the lawn is wetter than the path.» What does wetter mean in this sentence? | *More wet, with more water on it | Shinier and cleaner | Dryer and warmer | Lighter in weight
test: Ben says the rain today is wetter than yesterday's rain. What does he mean? | The rain is hotter today | Today has no rain at all | *There is more rain today | There is less rain today
exam: Write the correct word: «The towel I used to dry the dog is ___ than the towel I used to dry my hands.» | wettest | *wetter | wet | weter
